3780 - Associate Director, Media Planning, UK

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

The Media Planning Account Director works within a team of media planners with 1-3 direct reports, inspiring&nbsp;innovation&nbsp;and great thinking. Role will&nbsp;include:&nbsp;Strategic thinking, forecasting, weekly reporting&nbsp;reviews&nbsp;and campaign PCAs or QBRs. They will work with the team to ensure communication to the client is clear, compelling and of a high standard. The candidate will hold close client relationships and work alongside Client Services as the primary face of Essence’s acquisition media planning product for those clients. They will be&nbsp;ultimately responsible&nbsp;for campaign performance and the delivery of business-enhancing innovation. They will foster strong external relationships and keep a close eye on the market to ensure new opportunities and research are reviewed and implemented for the benefit of their clients. &nbsp;

You will be a key player in the planning team for Google Ads, defining contextual layers and precision of budgets across channels, and to help evolve best practice, including pushing the adoption of&nbsp;emerging&nbsp;technologies, leading the development and deployment of planning frameworks and the main POC for clients from planning. Managing the team to deliver planning and buying of activity. &nbsp;

Some of the things&nbsp;we’d&nbsp;like you to do: &nbsp;

• Be the point of contact for Planning across junior and&nbsp;mid level&nbsp;clients, lead weekly meetings with clients and presentations. &nbsp;

• Oversee and quality assure all deliverables produced by junior team members. &nbsp;

• Ensure the delivery of&nbsp;high quality&nbsp;strategic presentations, actionable weekly reporting, insightful post campaign&nbsp;analysis&nbsp;and clear briefs to Activation. &nbsp;

• Deliver clear and compelling rationale to support media investment recommendations and to evidence campaign performance versus expected outcomes. &nbsp;

• Work with Activation and Analytics to design the test and learn framework for assigned campaigns. &nbsp;

• Take responsibility for the performance of assigned media budgets against intended outcomes. &nbsp;

• Be a point of escalation for team issues (within and outside the team). &nbsp;

• Contribute to internal thought leadership and team process/workflow enhancement, increasing work quality, making us more efficient, and increasing Essential satisfaction. &nbsp;

• Set the quality standard for one or more planning deliverables per year, improving them over time via team/client feedback and incorporation of evolving external context. &nbsp;

Management Responsibility: &nbsp;

• Motivate a team, leading by example while coaching juniors. &nbsp;

• Provide&nbsp;timely&nbsp;and actionable feedback to aid in team development and improvement. &nbsp;

• Strong spreadsheet capability is&nbsp;a must, with a strong handle on using formulas and ideally able to use AI to build scripts. &nbsp;

• Monitor and support Essential satisfaction across client teams,&nbsp;identifying&nbsp;and implementing ways to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;or increase satisfaction. &nbsp;

• Foster strong working relationships across the client team to&nbsp;facilitate&nbsp;flawless execution of plans. &nbsp;

• Communicate effectively across all levels of the team.

SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.

SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We're creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.

SpaceXSI is hiring a Fleet Maintenance Supervisor for our AI supercompute facilities in Memphis. You will own fleet maintenance for automotive assets, heavy transit vehicles, trailers, UTVs, and industrial equipment. You will run the work-order schedule, cover emergency breakdowns, and occasionally do the work alongside your technicians. &nbsp;

This role requires 24/7 on-call coverage for critical breakdowns, and may include nights, weekends, and long hours with limited notice. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
RESPONSIBILITIES: &nbsp;

• Lead technicians through daily repairs, preventative maintenance, and continuous improvement projects, to increase uptime and ensure maximum asset availability across our Memphis facilities&nbsp;

• Set the weekly plan, assign work, and triage requests from internal customers by priority and available resources. &nbsp;

• Source third-party vendors for parts acquisition, documentation, training, and on-site repairs as needed

• Be the subject matter expert for all things related to the fleet &nbsp;

• Provide developmental leadership to technicians, facilitating training and advancement of skills

• Track team utilization and the maintenance KPIs used to improve uptime

• Facilitate all Title and Registration needs for the fleet

• Oversee the lifecycle of all fleet assets from acquisition through disposition

• Perform other related duties, as assigned, to ensure smooth operation of the fleet maintenance team &nbsp;

BASIC QUALIFICATIONS: &nbsp;

• High school diploma or equivalent.&nbsp;

• Functional knowledge of mechanical, electrical, hydraulic and pneumatic systems

• 4+ years maintaining or repairing vehicles, fleet equipment, or industrial equipment.

• 2+ years leading people, including assigning work and running maintenance jobs to completion. &nbsp;

PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE: &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline or completion of a related trade school

• ASE/OEM certifications &nbsp;

• Proficiency in Microsoft applications such as Excel, Outlook, Word, and PowerPoint

• Experience in a CMMS or other asset-management system &nbsp;

• Experience managing a maintenance budget, third-party vendors, and service contracts &nbsp;

• Ability to work independently with little direction

• Ability to meet deadlines in a fast-paced, ever-changing priorities environment

• Ability to anticipate needs and develop innovative solutions &nbsp;

• Ability to effectively communicate (verbal and written) with engineering, production, build, and support teams &nbsp;

ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS: &nbsp;

• Ability to lift 50 lbs. unassisted, lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position

• Must be willing to work at elevated heights and in tight spaces

• Must be willing to work long hours, nights, and weekends with limited notice to meet the business needs

• Provide 24/7 on-call support for all critical activities and emergency situations

• Willingness to travel to support the business &nbsp;

